      en: "Tenancingo is a historically rich municipality in the Cuscatlán Department, renowned nationwide for its artisanal production of high-quality palm hats. This traditional craft forms the backbone of the local economy and cultural identity. The town is nestled in a rugged, mountainous area, which historically made it a strategic and heavily contested location during the Salvadoran Civil War. It suffered severe damage and depopulation in 1983 but has since been rebuilt. Tenancingo is a profound case study in the resilience of artisanal traditions in the face of modern conflict and displacement."
